  "verbalization": "Norfloxacin appears to be indirectly linked to Rhinoscleroma through a series of bacterial infections that share a common pathway involving fluoroquinolones. The evidence suggests that Norfloxacin is associated with Chronic Tubotympanic Suppurative Otitis Media, which in turn is linked to Ofloxacin, and Ofloxacin further links to Rhinoscleroma. Similarly, Norfloxacin is also connected to Intestinal Infectious Disease, which is associated with Ciprofloxacin, and Ciprofloxacin is linked to Rhinoscleroma. These pathways highlight a potential mechanism where fluoroquinolones, such as Norfloxacin and Ofloxacin, are implicated in the development of Rhinoscleroma through their role in treating bacterial infections. The shared use of fluoroquinolones in these contexts suggests a possible overlap in their therapeutic effects, though the exact mechanism by which these infections lead to Rhinoscleroma remains unclear. The evidence supports a hypothesis that fluoroquinolone use may contribute to the development of Rhinoscleroma through the treatment of bacterial infections, but further research is needed to clarify the precise relationship.",
